# ferris_wheel:
# CSES 1090, Ferris Wheel (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1090), in our own words:
# children with given weights queue for a ferris wheel whose gondolas each hold one
# child or two, together at most x in weight; the fewest gondolas that carry every
# child. The input is the binary natural x (corpora/library/binary/natural) and a
# Scott list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of the weights, binary naturals, each at
# most x; the answer is a binary natural. Part of the CSES port's fourth batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: every way to partition the children into
# groups of one or two that fit is built (the first child is alone, or is paired with
# any later child whose weight fits with its own, the partition then going on with the
# others), the number of groups of each partition is listed, and the least is taken.
# Its reading builds every such partition, the matchings of the children, which grow
# faster than the factorial of half their number; the replacement the family asks for
# is to sort the weights and pair the lightest with the heaviest that fits, two
# pointers, in about n log n steps, on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application only:
# its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since the partitions
# of a list are built from the partitions of a shorter list, and every other recursion
# consumes a finite list; the branches that a Scott boolean discards are never read.
# The list of the numbers of groups is never empty, since a child alone is a group
# (each weight is at most x), so the least is taken of a nonempty list. The program
# calls no subtraction. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable
# equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an answer, P
# ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W, while Böhm's
# theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to λx y. y, and applying
# both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "pair")
λ pair _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ binary_minimum
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λ self least candidates. candidates least λ candidate rest. self (binary_minimum least candidate) rest
  )
λ fold_minimum
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self items
    . items nil
      λ head tail
      . cons (pair head tail) λ. map (λ picked. picked λ other rest. pair other (cons head rest)) λ. self tail
  )
λ picks
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λ self lists. lists nil λ head tail. append head λ. self tail
  )
λ flatten
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ capacity
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self children
        . children (cons binary_zero nil)
          λ head tail
          . append (map merge_binary_increment (self tail))
            λ. flatten
              ( map
                ( λ picked
                  . picked
                    λ other rest
                    . binary_less_than capacity (merge_binary_plus head other) nil (map merge_binary_increment (self rest))
                )
                (picks tail)
              )
      )
  )
λ group_counts
. (λtuple. tuple λcapacity children. (group_counts capacity children) binary_zero λhead tail. fold_minimum head tail)
λ ferris_wheel
. export ferris_wheel
